{"parentUuid":"62baa0db-30d9-41bb-9d59-7a481e76b56f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeLoLcDReHnvWVy6CoguY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's a draft built around those two value props with `sun init` as the fast on-ramp — I've written it to `README.md` so you can see it real, and flagged the decisions I want your input on below."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":100,"cache_read_input_tokens":297716,"output_tokens":3007,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1935},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":100,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3007,"cache_read_input_tokens":297716,"cache_creation_input_tokens":100,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":100},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeLoLAkVG78YsoyBh68ns","type":"assistant","uuid":"b99f4832-1db2-458c-ba44-b7a9caeae4c1","timestamp":"2026-08-24T02:40:25.118Z","effort":"high","session_id":"03b842fc-7029-49f7-afcc-ad7e2d3a1aea","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/bmo/sun","sessionId":"03b842fc-7029-49f7-afcc-ad7e2d3a1aea","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"b99f4832-1db2-458c-ba44-b7a9caeae4c1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeLoLcDReHnvWVy6CoguY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019US85aE1qwvK3jR5EBYj11","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /Users/bmo/sun/README.md <<'EOF'\n# sun\n\nYour repo has two histories: the code, and the conversations that produced it. git keeps the\nfirst and loses the second. sun keeps both — an operation log on top of git that records\n**who** made every change (you, a teammate, or a specific agent session), and stores the\nsessions themselves in the repo so your whole team's agents can use them.\n\n## One command\n\n```sh\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sundial-org/sun/main/install.sh | sh\ncd your-repo && sun init\n```\n\n`sun init` imports every Claude Code session that ever touched this repo (worktrees and\nsubagents included), backfills attribution across your existing commits, and ends with a\nlink to an HTML replay of your history. 6,489 commits + 33 MB of transcripts import in\n6.4s; reruns take 0.7s. From then on, hooks keep the log current automatically: one commit\nper agent tool call, squashed to one commit per turn, human edits detected jj-style between.\n\n## 1 · Analyze your past sessions\n\n| command | what you learn |\n| --- | --- |\n| `sun log` | git log annotated with actors, sessions and turn numbers |\n| `sun show <commit>` | the events behind a commit — patches, tool calls, session — even after a squash-merge (patch-id) |\n| `sun viz` | self-contained HTML: branches, commits, operations, replay from the beginning |\n| `sun sessions [id] [--grep re] [--file p]` | list, read and search every session that ran here |\n| `sun undo [--op ID] [--commit H]` | reverse any single operation or commit |\n\n## 2 · Share sessions with your team's agents\n\nSessions live as git objects under `refs/sun/*` — never in your worktree, invisible to\n`git status` and PR diffs — and travel with plain `git push` / `git pull`. On a teammate's\nclone, `sun init` surfaces them, and their agents are pointed at `.git/sun/sessions/` (the\nexact `~/.claude/projects` layout, now including teammates' sessions) via a `SessionStart`\ncontext line and one line in `CLAUDE.md`. Agents debugging auth can read the session where\nauth was built — whoever's machine it ran on. No server, no LFS, nothing to operate.\n\n`sun sync` · `sun import` · `sun gc --older-than N` · `sun hook` round out the CLI.\n\n## Demos & tests\n\n```sh\npython3 example/demo_init.py   # pick any repo you've used Claude Code on -> timed sun init\npython3 example/demo_fresh.py  # synthetic end-to-end story -> example/demo.html\npython3 -m unittest test_sun   # 33 tests\n```\nEOF\nwc -l /Users/bmo/sun/README.md","description":"Draft value-prop-focused README"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":100,"cache_read_input_tokens":297716,"output_tokens":3007,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1935},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":100,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3007,"cache_read_input_tokens":297716,"cache_creation_input_tokens":100,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":100},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeLoLAkVG78YsoyBh68ns","type":"assistant","uuid":"83d1aafc-59ae-4f11-9ca0-e536828f0c4b","timestamp":"2026-08-24T02:40:34.245Z","effort":"high","session_id":"03b842fc-7029-49f7-afcc-ad7e2d3a1aea","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/bmo/sun","sessionId":"03b842fc-7029-49f7-afcc-ad7e2d3a1aea","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"main"}
